# Line-ending policy for scripts.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. That corrupts the shebang of every POSIX script in the tree, so a
# clone made on Windows cannot run the build documented in docs/COMPILATION.MD
# or the local-source Docker build in docker/README.md:
#
#     $ ./pre-build.sh
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#     exit=127
#
# Pin these to LF on every platform. Deliberately narrow: no "* text=auto",
# because many tracked files are committed with CRLF and normalising them all
# would be a repo-wide rewrite unrelated to this fix.

*.sh            text eol=lf
*.command       text eol=lf

linux/build             text eol=lf
linux/build_hardsubx    text eol=lf
linux/builddebug        text eol=lf
linux/cleanup           text eol=lf
linux/module_generator  text eol=lf

mac/cleanup             text eol=lf
mac/gui/src/CCExtractor.app/Contents/Resources/script text eol=lf

# The mirror case: Windows batch and PowerShell scripts want CRLF.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.ps1           text eol=crlf
